            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0694" n="612" xml:id="pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1170: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-12T13:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 12,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:23 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>559. Your 421, November 11, 5 p.m. I have always had a perfect understanding of
                    the attitude of the American Government regarding the service of American
                    citizens in armed forces in Morocco, and I have governed myself accordingly. I
                    have never at any time had any sort of communication with them nor has there
                    ever been any question of any sort of official recognition. In fact I fail to
                    understand the cause of your 421.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
